\name{cellucid_dataset_summary}
\alias{cellucid_dataset_summary}
\title{Read the dataset summary}
\usage{
cellucid_dataset_summary(viewer)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{cells}, \code{citation}, \code{embeddings}, \code{fields}, \code{genes}, \code{id} (The dataset's id where it has one), \code{name}, \code{source} (Where it was opened from (a sample, a link, a local file, a notebook)). Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
The open dataset: its name, citation, how many cells (and how many are open), genes, embeddings and fields.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{dataset.summary} (Dataset). It reads, and changes nothing: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_dataset_summary(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for what it read.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
